{"availability":"available","full":"gokhanercan/gen-atomic","name":"gen-atomic","description":"An LLM-based code generation framework aims to support a wide range of atomic language units, from compiled code to semi-structured markups.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":9,"forks":0,"created":"2024-04-01T08:40:30Z","updated":"2025-10-14T16:57:04Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["benchmark","code-generation","gen-ai","llm"],"demo":"https://gen-atomic.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:13.438Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:13.438Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:13.438Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T05:50:13.438Z","stars":9,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Gen-atomic is an LLM-based code generation and evaluation framework that aims to support a wide range of atomic language units (e.g., C#, Python, SQL, Regex, React, YAML, D2Lang), from compiled code to semi-structured markups. It allows developers to easily create an evaluation framework for a specific language or framework without needing deep knowledge of LLM concepts such as RAG, prompting, or benchmarking.","It also serves as a runtime library that enables developers to generate code blocks using the best available model configurations for a given language or framework. It collects data from offline experiments to maximize runtime performance by determining which models to use and how to ensemble them for a particular task, based on defined cost, time, and performance goals.","The ultimate client usage will be as follows:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gokhanercan/gen-atomic/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"f2308d2c1e25bbfa55e30ac9edde39c4bb048a0a0edd7f88de97fb49d51fb588","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:14.185Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:14.185Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Gen-atomic is an LLM-based code generation and evaluation framework that aims to support a wide range of atomic language units (e.g., C#, Python, SQL, Regex, React, YAML, D2Lang), from compiled code to semi-structured markups. It allows developers to easily create an evaluation framework for a specific language or framework without needing deep knowledge of LLM concepts such as RAG, prompting, or benchmarking.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gokhanercan/gen-atomic/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Gen-atomic is an LLM-based code generation and evaluation framework that aims to support a wide range of atomic language units (e.g., C#, Python, SQL, Regex, React, YAML, D2Lang), from compiled code to semi-structured markups. It allows developers to easily create an evaluation framework for a specific language or framework without needing deep knowledge of LLM concepts such…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gokhanercan/gen-atomic/blob/master/README.md"},{"text":"It also serves as a runtime library that enables developers to generate code blocks using the best available model configurations for a given language or framework. It collects data from offline experiments to maximize runtime performance by determining which models to use and how to ensemble them for a particular task, based on defined cost, time, and performance goals.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gokhanercan/gen-atomic/blob/master/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f2308d2c1e25bbfa55e30ac9edde39c4bb048a0a0edd7f88de97fb49d51fb588","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gokhanercan/gen-atomic/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:14.185Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-10-14T16:57:04Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gokhanercan/gen-atomic/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:14.186Z","hash":"f2308d2c1e25bbfa55e30ac9edde39c4bb048a0a0edd7f88de97fb49d51fb588","originalBytes":6066,"storedBytes":6066,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["project","code","r